  <data name="Autostart_UnsafeFolder_ResetAsk" xml:space="preserve"><value>tomodachi is under Program Files, but programs without admin rights can still change these files:

{0}

This usually happens when the folder was moved there instead of copied: a move keeps the old permissions.

Autostart runs tomodachi with admin rights and without asking. Any program running under your account could replace the exe or a DLL there and would get admin rights at the next start.

tomodachi can reset the permissions now. Afterwards they are the same as for the rest of Program Files, like after a fresh install.

Reset permissions and set up autostart?</value></data>
