{0}</value></data>
  <data name="Autostart_UnsafeFolder_Move" xml:space="preserve"><value>Recommended: copy the tomodachi folder to Program Files or unzip it there (don't move it, a move keeps the old permissions), then turn on autostart from there.</value></data>
  <data name="Autostart_UnsafeFolder_Reset" xml:space="preserve"><value>tomodachi could not reset the permissions automatically. You can do it by hand in an admin PowerShell and then turn on autostart again (Ctrl+C copies this whole message):

icacls "{0}" /setowner *S-1-5-32-544 /T /C
icacls "{0}" /reset /T /C</value></data>
